WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
The last scene.

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.110
An old man kneels over a still figure.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.780
A friend asks, "Is this the promis’d end?"

4
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.470
Behind them, readers line
up across the centuries:

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:19.250
1681, 1765, 1904, 1964.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.450
Each one holds up a verdict, face down.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.350
Four hundred years of readers.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.740
So, after all that suffering,
is there any comfort here?

9
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.700
In this mission, you'll meet a
1681 rewrite with a happy ending,

10
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.700
where Lear is restored.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.500
Then you'll test Bradley, Kott and the
critics who followed on that same ending.

12
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.530
Your mission: decide whether
King Lear offers any comfort.
